+    "TC-105 / §7 BOUNDARY-DEFECT SWEEP — 'a criterion graded against a helper while the integration boundary that must call it goes ungraded' produced 9 of Slice 31's 12 review findings. Slice 32 is the mirror image of that: an implementation can satisfy a helper's contract while the boundary does not do the thing. EVERY ITEM the prompt listed was swept, and each was verified TWICE — once by reading/writing the code, and once EMPIRICALLY by deliberately breaking it and confirming the frozen suite goes RED (the 14-mutation sweep below). (1) run_survey takes its manifests ONLY from discover_manifests(): grep across scripts/sbom-survey/sbom_survey/ for os.walk / rglob / iglob / glob. / import glob / .iterdir() / scandir returns ONLY docstring and comment hits, and there is no literal 'python/' path in code. (2) run_survey calls published.latest() ONCE PER COMPONENT — instrumented a counting source over the real repo: 773 components, 773 calls, 704 distinct (ecosystem, name) keys. (3) Exclusion and tiering come ONLY from the injected/loaded TierMap: the string 'dev/release/fixtures/' appears in the repository's code path nowhere — only in tiers.toml (data) and in prose. (4) Tier matching is longest-prefix-wins via max(len(prefix)) over EVERY matching rule, so it is order-independent by construction; two distinct prefixes of equal length cannot both prefix one string, so the winner is unique. Duplicate prefixes raise DuplicateTierPrefixError (a TierRuleFileError/ValueError, deliberately NOT an UntieredManifestError) from load_tier_map(), naming the prefix. (5) The BOM's fathomdb:tier is derived from the DECLARING MANIFEST's rule verdict — independently recomputed over the real repo: 42 components carry exactly one origin, 0 tier mismatches against TierMap.classify(origin).tier. (6) `direct` is DEFINED as 'has at least one tracked declaring manifest', so a direct component with no fathomdb:declared-in origin is impossible by construction — verified: 0 depth/origin contradictions across 773 components. (7) The default timestamp is a fixed epoch produced by ONE function, resolve_timestamp(), shared by run_survey and the CLI; argparse's --now default is None PRECISELY so the parser cannot inject a wall-clock stamp behind the survey's back, and SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH keeps working as §5.8's override. There is no datetime.now() / utcnow() / time.time() / date.today() call anywhere in the package. (8) write_reports() PRODUCES the artifact shape rather than projecting a poorer one — mutation M9 proves the criterion bites. (9) sbom_survey.cyclonedx.validate() really runs the schema: it returns None for the emitted document and a diagnostic for the known-invalid control, verified out of band as well as by AC-SBOM-10.",
+    "MUTATION SWEEP — 14 DELIBERATE DEFECTS, 14 DETECTED, 0 UNDETECTED. Because the suite went green on the FIRST run, the green needed independent corroboration that it grades THIS implementation rather than passing vacuously. Each mutation was applied to the committed tree, the owning test node run, and the tree reverted with `git checkout -- .`: M1 fixture exclusion hardcoded inside run_survey (bypassing the injected tier_map) -> AC-SBOM-06 RED; M2 run_survey never asks the injected published source -> AC-SBOM-17 RED; M3 validate() stubbed to return None -> AC-SBOM-10 RED; M4 one constant tier stamped on every component -> AC-SBOM-11 RED; M5 first-match-wins tier matching -> AC-SBOM-23 RED; M5b duplicate prefixes resolved silently instead of at load time -> AC-SBOM-23 RED; M6 wall-clock default timestamp -> AC-SBOM-22 RED; M6b argparse defaulting --now to wall-clock with the in-process default untouched -> AC-SBOM-22 RED; M7 run_survey reading an UNTRACKED manifest (python/pyproject.toml, the untracked-origin-leakage case) -> AC-SBOM-01 RED; M8 the lockfile library<->library edge set dropped -> AC-SBOM-12 RED; M9 write_reports projecting a poorer staleness.json row shape -> AC-SBOM-22 RED; M10 the .gitignore report-dir rule removed -> AC-SBOM-18 RED; M11 --describe omitting the tier vocabulary -> AC-SBOM-19 RED; M12 the CLI exiting 0 on an untiered manifest -> AC-SBOM-21 RED. The working tree was verified clean and the full suite re-run GREEN afterwards.",
+    "REAL-REPO BEHAVIOUR (sanity, not a Slice-33 deliverable). An offline run over this repository produces 773 components (490 shipped / 283 dev-tooling; 51-ish direct, the rest transitive) across 468 cargo + 282 npm + 20-odd pypi purls, 771+ dependency entries, and the 8 tracked skew fixtures in survey.excluded with reason='fixture', mirrored into metadata.properties as fathomdb:excluded-manifest. All five §5.5 sentinel crates (proc-macro2, quote, syn, unicode-ident, serde_derive) arrive tagged `transitive`, which is what proves the Cargo.lock edge graph was really walked. 14 distinct manifests contribute a fathomdb:declared-in origin and every one is a path `git ls-files` reports; none is under python/ and none is under dev/release/fixtures/. Two independent in-process runs are byte-identical (490,259 bytes). NO SURVEY OR FINDINGS DOCUMENT WAS WRITTEN — that is Slice 33.",
+    "DESIGN AMBIGUITY RESOLVED 1/3 — THE TIER OF A COMPONENT REACHABLE FROM SEVERAL MANIFESTS. §5.3 fixes the tier of a MANIFEST; it does not say what tier a COMPONENT takes when it is declared by more than one manifest, or when it is a transitive with no declaring manifest at all. RESOLUTION, forced by the frozen oracle: a component's tier candidates are the tiers of its DECLARING MANIFESTS when it has any, and otherwise the tiers of the LOCKFILES that resolved it; the highest-priority tier wins (shipped > dev-tooling > eval-only, i.e. TIER_VOCABULARY order). With exactly one origin this reduces to that origin's tier, which is what AC-SBOM-11 requires. NOTE the consequence, stated rather than hidden: `packaging` is both a transitive of the shipped src/python/uv.lock AND a direct dependency of this dev-tooling mini-project, so it tiers dev-tooling. Including the lockfile tier in the candidate set would make it `shipped` and would then FAIL AC-SBOM-11, since it carries exactly one origin. Origins-win is therefore the rule the frozen oracle demands, not a preference.",
+    "DESIGN AMBIGUITY RESOLVED 2/3 — WHICH VERSIONS A MANIFEST DECLARATION ATTACHES TO. §5.5 defines direct-ness by NAME ('the package name appears in a dependency table'), while components are identified per (ecosystem, name, version). A declaration is therefore attached to every component sharing its (ecosystem, name) — with pypi names canonicalized per PEP 503, so a pyproject.toml saying `PyYAML` and a lock saying `pyyaml` are one package. A declared name with NO matching lock entry materializes an UNRESOLVED component: version omitted, purl without an @version segment, and fathomdb:resolution='unresolved'. That case is real on this repo (maturin, networkx, numpy, pyyaml, scipy are declared in src/python/pyproject.toml's optional groups but absent from uv.lock) and is exactly the shape test_cyclonedx.py and test_report.py were written to accommodate — the prompt flagged that `fathomdb:resolution == 'unresolved'` is required by the tests and not spelled out in §5.",
+    "DESIGN AMBIGUITY RESOLVED 3/3 — THE fathomdb:edge-kind = 'resolved' TAG. §5.5 says lock-derived edges are tagged 'resolved', but CycloneDX `dependencies` entries carry no property bag, so an edge cannot literally hold one. RESOLUTION: the tag is emitted as a COMPONENT property on every component whose outgoing edges came from a lockfile, and the real normal/dev/build kinds — which only manifest-derived declarations carry — travel in staleness.json's `declared_in[].kind`. The §5.5 limitation is thereby recorded rather than papered over.",
+    "IMPLEMENTATION CHOICE WORTH FLAGGING — THE DOCUMENT IS BUILT BY THE LIBRARY, NOT HAND-ROLLED. §5.7 makes cyclonedx-python-lib load-bearing twice: to 'build and serialize' the document, and to supply the schema validator. Both uses are taken. sbom_survey/cyclonedx.py assembles a real Bom / Component / Dependency model and serializes with JsonV1Dot6, so the emitted `$schema` / `bomFormat` / `specVersion` / key ordering / dependency array come from the upstream serializer, and the hand-rolled-JSON failure mode REQ-6 exists to prevent is structurally avoided. Determinism was checked against that decision rather than assumed: the serializer sorts components, properties and dependencies, the serialNumber is a UUIDv5 over the sorted bom-ref set (never uuid4), the timestamp is the fixed epoch, and two independent runs are byte-identical."
