The survey can produce incorrect direct/transitive classification and declared constraints for packages with multiple locked versions, which affects the main staleness output this tool is meant to feed to the next slice.

Review comment:

- [P2] Avoid attaching declarations to every locked version — /home/coreyt/projects/fathomdb-worktrees/slice-32-sbom-code/scripts/sbom-survey/sbom_survey/survey.py:331-344
  When a lockfile contains multiple versions of the same package name, this name-only lookup marks all versions as declared by the manifest, even if the manifest constraint can only resolve to one of them. In the current repo this makes `sha2 0.10.9` carry origins whose constraint is `0.11`, and similarly marks both `thiserror` and `tokenizers` versions as direct, so Slice 33 would see misleading direct dependencies and edit sites for versions that are actually transitive. The declaration should be matched to the resolved lock entry when the lockfile disambiguates the version, rather than to every build with the same `(ecosystem, name)`.
